Send the `Accept` and `Sec-Fetch-Mode` headers a browser would send when checking an external link, alongside the browser user agent that was already used. Without them some servers reject the request and the link is reported as broken although it works for a human: `www.edvance.it` negotiates on `Accept` and answers 404 to the `*/*` requests sends by default, while `facebook.com` answers 400 to a client that claims to be a browser without the metadata a real navigation carries.
